ng extensive regional mandates such as Peppol BIS 3.0 self-billing. Based on primary research, the company has not disclosed explicit technical transaction throughput scalability benchmarks or specific service level agreement (SLA) percentage metrics for system uptime within its public product specifications. customer.basware.com +1"}}}, "y": {"score": 92, "axis": "Business Strength", "composite_reported": 92, "evidence": [{"claim": "Processed more than two billion invoices to date and handled $10.1 trillion in business spend as of February 2025."}, {"claim": "Awarded three government contracts worth $12,643,502 via its subsidiary Basware Pty Ltd."}, {"claim": "Generated an estimated annual revenue of $181.6 million as of September 2025."}, {"claim": "Achieved a 52% growth in commercial bookings during its global expansion drive."}, {"claim": "Provides global invoice automation coverage across 100+ countries with over 250 ERP integrations and 220 interoperability partners."}, {"claim": "Expanded global consultancy capabilities through strategic alliances with Accenture, Deloitte, Capgemini, and KPMG."}, {"claim": "Maintained an enterprise market footprint supported by a global workforce of 1,316 employees."}, {"claim": "Achieved a Tracxn competitiveness score of 61/100, ranking as a prominent late-stage provider in the global AP automation market."}, {"claim": "Completed 10 financing rounds and raised a total of $413 million in venture capital backing."}, {"claim": "Executed sequential strategic acquisitions including Glantus Holdings in 2023, AP Matching in 2024, Redmap Australia in 2025, and a binding agreement to acquire Trustpair in August 2026."}], "parameters": {"Customer Base & Contract Wins": {"score": 68, "evidence": [{"claim": "The company reports serving over 6,500 global customers, retaining 98% of its overall client base, and maintaining a 100% retention rate for its top 70 customers over a three-year period."}, {"claim": "The company reports enterprise